<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 5 September, from 394 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/394">394 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,632 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of the Frigidus opens between Theodosius I and Eugenius</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the river Frigidus, probably the Vipava in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, the western usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenius">Eugenius</a> and his Frankish general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arbogast">Arbogast</a> held their positions against the eastern emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> on the first day of battle. Theodosius won on the second.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus">Battle of the Frigidus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/917">917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Liu Yan proclaims himself emperor, founding the Southern Han</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Liu Yan, military governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingnan">Lingnan</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a> in succession to his brother Liu Yin, proclaimed himself emperor of Great Yue, renaming the state Han the next year. Southern Han, one of the Ten Kingdoms, lived on the sea trade.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-yan-southern-han">Liu Yan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1367">1367 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">659 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swa Saw Ke becomes king of Ava in Upper Burma</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swa-saw-ke">Swa Saw Ke</a> became king of Ava, the kingdom founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thado-minbya">Thado Minbya</a> in 1365, and restored central authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a> for the first time since the fall of Pagan. In 1385 he began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forty-years-war">Forty Years' War</a> against Hanthawaddy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swa-saw-ke">Swa Saw Ke</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1698">1698 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">328 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter the Great shaves his nobles' beards</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Back from his Grand Embassy to western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, Peter I personally cut off the beards of leading boyars. A tax on beards followed, part of his drive to westernise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s elite.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1774">1774 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">252 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Continental Congress meets in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from twelve colonies gathered at Carpenters' Hall to coordinate resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intolerable-acts">Intolerable Acts</a>. They agreed a boycott of British goods and planned to meet again.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crazy Horse is killed at Camp Robinson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Oglala Lakota leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crazy-horse">Crazy Horse</a>, a victor at Little Bighorn, was bayoneted by a soldier while resisting arrest at Camp Robinson, Nebraska. He died that night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Palestinian gunmen seize Israeli athletes at the Munich Olympics</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-september">Black September</a> militants killed two members of the Israeli team and took nine hostage. All nine and a West German policeman died in a failed rescue at Fürstenfeldbruck airbase.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lynette Fromme tries to shoot President Ford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Manson Family follower Lynette 'Squeaky' Fromme aimed a pistol at Gerald Ford in Sacramento, but no round was chambered. A second attempt on Ford came 17 days later.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 5 September <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-viii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-viii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis VIII of France</span><span class="tp">1187–1226</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-iv-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-iv-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter IV of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1319–1387</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/date-masamune"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/date-masamune.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Date Masamune</span><span class="tp">1567–1636</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-christian-elector-of-saxony"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-christian-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick Christian, Elector of Saxony</span><span class="tp">1722–1763</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 5 September <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/authari"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/authari.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Authari</span><span class="tp">d. 590</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-i-duke-of-brabant"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-i-duke-of-brabant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry I, Duke of Brabant</span><span class="tp">1165–1235</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-aba"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-aba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amadeus Aba</span><span class="tp">d. 1311</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/crazy-horse"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Crazy Horse</span><span class="tp">c. 1840–1877</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arthur-macarthur-jr"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arthur-macarthur-jr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arthur MacArthur Jr.</span><span class="tp">1845–1912</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
